1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,667
Dad, if we eat turkey, does that mean we go to church?

2
00:00:02,667 --> 00:00:08,167
Of course! Thanksgiving is church Chuseok! Turkey is church-only chicken!

3
00:00:08,167 --> 00:00:10,700
A turkey's just a bird. Anyone can eat it.

4
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:11,400
…Huh?

5
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:15,367
Wrong answer number one. I'm Modapman.

6
00:00:17,067 --> 00:00:21,900
Case summary. Thanksgiving shopping. Location: the meat counter.

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,033
Mister, what's this green stamp?

8
00:00:24,067 --> 00:00:29,233
Halal. It means the meat was prepared by Islamic rules.

9
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:33,100
Grandma goes to Catholic Mass, my uncle goes to a Protestant church. Different religions?

10
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:37,833
Sure. Mass is Catholic, church is Christian. Totally different.

11
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:40,200
Both are Christian. Brothers from the same family.

12
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:42,567
Wha? Wha? Wha? Wha… AAAH!

13
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:46,267
Wrong answer, two. Mom the model answer, out ten minutes into shopping.

14
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:50,000
My uncle talked about 'idan.' What's that?

15
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,100
Idan, like the jump kick! One jump, two kicks!

16
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:56,367
Different, and end. It means 'different at the core.' It's the word for heresy.

17
00:00:56,367 --> 00:01:00,733
Wrong answer, three. Dad kicked thin air at the meat counter.

18
00:01:00,767 --> 00:01:02,500
Okay. Just three rounds.

19
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:04,267
You count meat by the pound, though…

20
00:01:04,267 --> 00:01:10,167
Round one. Judaism, Christianity, Islam. All three honor Abraham as their forefather.

21
00:01:10,167 --> 00:01:13,767
They split on one thing. Who Jesus is.

22
00:01:13,767 --> 00:01:19,200
Judaism: the savior hasn't come yet. Christianity: Jesus is the Son of God.

23
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:23,833
Islam: Jesus is a great prophet, and the last prophet is Muhammad.

24
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:30,167
Their books: the Hebrew Bible, the Bible, the Quran. Their holy days: Saturday, Sunday, Friday.

25
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:33,833
Join all three and… a three-day weekend!

26
00:01:33,833 --> 00:01:39,167
Judaism and Islam don't eat pork. Meat made by their rules is kosher, or halal.

27
00:01:39,167 --> 00:01:40,600
So that's the green stamp!

28
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:46,133
Round two. Inside Christianity, three big branches. Catholic, Orthodox, Protestant.

29
00:01:46,133 --> 00:01:49,633
Five hundred years ago, a priest named Luther said, 'Back to the Bible.'

30
00:01:49,633 --> 00:01:54,233
Ah, a remodel! Protestants are the remodeled Catholics!

31
00:01:54,233 --> 00:01:59,433
…Half right. The Korean word does mean 'fix and renew.'

32
00:01:59,433 --> 00:02:02,700
Wrong answer, one half. Rounded up: four.

33
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:08,133
Catholics look to the Bible plus the church's long tradition. Protestants: the Bible alone.

34
00:02:08,133 --> 00:02:12,900
Catholic churches have priests, Protestant churches have pastors. Priests don't marry.

35
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:13,833
What about pastors?

36
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:14,767
They can.

37
00:02:14,933 --> 00:02:21,033
Round three. Protestants have lots of families too. Presbyterian, Methodist, Baptist…

38
00:02:21,033 --> 00:02:24,533
Like our Mo family! Same last name, different ancestral clans!

39
00:02:24,533 --> 00:02:29,400
Exactly. Presbyterians began with Calvin, Methodists with Wesley.

40
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:33,200
They believe almost the same things. They differ in who leads: a council of elders, or bishops.

41
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:37,067
'Methodist' was a nickname. Friends teased them for living by strict methods.

42
00:02:37,067 --> 00:02:40,067
Living by the rules, model student… that's supposed to be my job.

43
00:02:40,067 --> 00:02:44,667
In 1885, on Easter, a missionary from each family arrived in Korea on the same boat.

44
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:45,933
Then what's heresy?

45
00:02:45,933 --> 00:02:50,333
Groups that church bodies have ruled differ on core teachings, like who Jesus is.

46
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:55,933
In one line: how they see Jesus, what they go by, and how they run the church.

47
00:02:56,033 --> 00:02:58,067
They're all different. So why are they all thankful?

48
00:02:58,067 --> 00:03:01,000
They believe different things, but feeling grateful is pretty much the same.

49
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,800
That's why we never make fun of what others believe. Like following the rules at a friend's house.

50
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,700
Then when Hasan next door comes over, let's get meat with the green stamp.

51
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:11,700
My kid looked for the green stamps, one by one.

52
00:03:11,867 --> 00:03:15,333
Dad, so what religion is our family?

53
00:03:15,333 --> 00:03:17,567
Our family? We're the Mo family, so… Mo-ism! (In Korean, 'mogyo' means your old school.)

54
00:03:17,567 --> 00:03:19,267
That's the school you graduated from.

55
00:03:19,267 --> 00:03:21,567
Wrong answer, five. Modapman strikes again.
